  <div class="pod-copy l-en">
    <p>That changes the way the forecast must be constructed.</p>
    <p>The lesson is not that timing is impossible and therefore useless.</p>
    <p>The lesson is that <strong>causal conditions must outrank calendar analogies</strong>.</p>
    <p>If the condition that was supposed to arrive in October appears in August, the forecast should move to August.</p>
    <p>If the market begins pricing a future policy architecture before the policy itself is implemented, we should not wait for the official meeting date to acknowledge it.</p>
    <p>If a stock peaks while the industry it belongs to remains fundamentally strong, we should stop pretending one "cycle" controls both.</p>
    <p>That is the repair being made in this report.</p>
    <p>The previous framework was strongest at identifying the forces and the relative winners.</p>
    <p>It was weaker at identifying when those forces would become dominant.</p>
    <p>So the new framework is not organized around a predetermined month-by-month path.</p>
    <p>It is organized around <strong>regimes, triggers and reaction functions</strong>.</p>
    <p>The dates still matter where real events are scheduled: inflation releases, Treasury buybacks, Federal Reserve meetings, Bank of Japan decisions, stablecoin implementation milestones and earnings reports.</p>
    <p>But the calendar no longer gets to overrule the evidence.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pod-copy l-zh">
    <p>这改变了预测必须被构建的方式。</p>
    <p>教训不是择时不可能、所以毫无用处。</p>
    <p>教训是：<strong>因果条件的权威必须高于日历类比</strong>。</p>
    <p>如果原本应该在 10 月出现的条件在 8 月就出现，预测就应该移到 8 月。</p>
    <p>如果市场在政策真正实施前就开始为未来政策架构定价，我们不应该等到正式会议日期才承认它。</p>
    <p>如果一只股票见顶时，它所在行业的基本面仍然强劲，我们就不该继续假装一只“周期”控制两者。</p>
    <p>这正是本报告所做的修正。</p>
    <p>旧框架最擅长识别驱动力与相对赢家。</p>
    <p>它更不擅长识别这些驱动力何时会占据主导。</p>
    <p>因此，新框架不再围绕一条预先设定的逐月路径组织。</p>
    <p>它围绕<strong>体制、触发器与反应函数</strong>组织。</p>
    <p>真实事件排定的日期依旧重要：通胀数据、美债回购、美联储会议、日本央行决议、稳定币实施里程碑与财报。</p>
    <p>但日历不再拥有推翻证据的权力。</p>
  </div>

