  <h2 id="assets"><span class="num">8</span>{{ t('Hard assets and crypto', '硬资产与加密资产') }}</h2>
  <div class="pod-copy">
    <p>{{ t('A regime centered on the price of duration naturally pushes investors toward assets that appear to sit outside long-duration nominal claims. That creates a temptation to group everything together: gold, silver, Bitcoin, platinum, palladium, copper—“hard assets” and “debasement trades.” That language is useful at a distance. It becomes dangerous up close.',
      '以久期价格为中心的体制，天然把投资者推向看似位于长期名义债权之外的资产，于是人们很容易把黄金、白银、比特币、铂金、钯金与铜统称为“硬资产”或“贬值交易”。这种语言远看有用，近看危险。') }}</p>
    <p>{{ t('These assets respond to very different combinations of real rates, liquidity, industrial demand, physical scarcity and risk appetite. The right question is not: <strong>Which hard asset is best?</strong> It is: <strong>Which asset is expressing which part of the regime?</strong>',
      '这些资产回应实际利率、流动性、工业需求、物理稀缺与风险偏好的不同组合。正确问题不是<strong>哪种硬资产最好？</strong>而是：<strong>哪种资产正在表达体制的哪一部分？</strong>') }}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pod-copy l-en">
    <h3>Gold: the cleanest signal</h3>
    <p>Gold is the most important asset in the current report because its behavior changed before the rest of the macro framework did.</p>
    <p>Our earlier thesis assumed that gold's durable next leg would probably require a cleaner path toward lower real yields and eventual Federal Reserve easing. Instead, gold accelerated while long-term nominal yields remained high and real yields were still restrictive.</p>
    <p>That means the market added something to the equation. Gold is no longer trading only on: real rates; the dollar; central-bank demand; and geopolitical reserve diversification. It is increasingly trading on uncertainty over <strong>how the long-duration financing problem will ultimately be resolved</strong>. That is a subtle but important distinction.</p>
    <p>If a high Treasury yield represents attractive real compensation and policy credibility, gold should face a headwind. If the high yield represents increasing compensation for fiscal or duration risk, gold can rise alongside it. The nominal yield looks the same. The message inside it is different. That is why the combination of long yields and the dollar matters so much.</p>
    <h3>Gold is not a one-way trade</h3>
    <p>The structural thesis has strengthened. The tactical setup can still be poor after a vertical rally.</p>
    <p>If inflation remains hot and the Fed responds by forcing real yields higher, gold can correct sharply. If the dollar rallies with real yields, the correction can be violent.</p>
    <p>That does not automatically invalidate the long-run thesis. It means the path to a larger monetary adjustment can include a period where the central bank successfully tightens.</p>
    <p>This is why we prefer to treat gold as the <strong>signal asset</strong>. It is the cleanest way to observe whether the market is becoming less comfortable with long-duration nominal claims. But even the cleanest signal can become overbought. Structural conviction is not a substitute for entry discipline.</p>
    <h3>Silver: monetary beta with an industrial engine</h3>
    <p>Silver is often described as gold with more upside. That is too simple.</p>
    <p>Silver contains a monetary component and a meaningful industrial component. That gives it more convexity in a benign easing regime. If real yields fall, the dollar weakens and global activity remains healthy, silver can outperform gold substantially.</p>
    <p>But the same structure makes it more vulnerable in a credit accident. Industrial demand expectations can fall. Leverage can unwind. Liquidity can disappear. Silver can drop much faster than gold.</p>
    <p>That is why our hierarchy is: <strong>Gold = cleaner monetary signal. Silver = higher-beta monetary expression.</strong> The two should not be treated as interchangeable.</p>
    <h3>Platinum and palladium: the labels hide the fundamentals</h3>
    <p>Platinum and palladium are both grouped into the precious-metals complex. Their physical outlooks are increasingly different.</p>
    <p>Platinum has a more attractive medium-term supply-demand balance, with constrained inventories and a stronger probability of persistent deficits. Palladium faces a more difficult structural backdrop because of the long-run transition in automotive demand and the possibility of surplus.</p>
    <p>That makes our preferred relative view: <strong>Platinum over palladium.</strong></p>
    <p>This is not a prediction that platinum rises every month or that palladium cannot squeeze. Palladium can rally violently on supply disruptions, short covering or geopolitical events. But a tactical squeeze and a structural deficit are not the same investment thesis. The important point is that the PGM complex should be analyzed through physical balances rather than the word "precious."</p>
    <h3>Copper: the best structural story can still be a bad entry</h3>
    <p>Copper remains one of the strongest long-run industrial scarcity stories in the portfolio. The demand case is unusually broad. AI data centers require electrical infrastructure. Grids require reinforcement. Power generation requires transmission. Robotics requires motors and wiring. Electrification requires copper. Defense requires copper. Mine supply takes years to develop.</p>
    <p>That is a powerful long-term setup. But a strong secular story does not make every price attractive.</p>
    <p>The recent copper squeeze demonstrated that physical tightness, warehouse positioning and speculative structure can push the market far beyond what a long-term investor should comfortably chase.</p>
    <p>This is another recurring lesson in the report: <strong>structural scarcity and tactical entry are different questions.</strong></p>
    <p>The best copper opportunity may come after the market digests an acute squeeze rather than during it. The thesis remains strong. The urgency does not.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pod-copy l-zh">
    <h3>黄金：最干净的信号</h3>
    <p>黄金是本报告最重要的资产，因为它的行为先于宏观框架其他部分发生变化。</p>
    <p>旧论点假设，黄金下一段持久上涨大概需要一条更清晰的实际收益率下降与美联储最终宽松路径。事实却是，长期名义收益率仍高、实际收益率仍具限制性时，黄金就已加速。</p>
    <p>这意味着市场向方程加入了新变量。黄金不再只交易实际利率、美元、央行需求与地缘政治储备多元化，而是越来越多地交易<strong>长久期融资问题最终将如何解决</strong>的不确定性。</p>
    <p>如果高美债收益率代表有吸引力的实际补偿与政策信誉，黄金理应受压；如果它代表财政或久期风险补偿提高，黄金可以与收益率一起上涨。名义收益率看起来相同，里面的信息不同。所以长端收益率与美元的组合极其重要。</p>
    <h3>黄金不是单边交易</h3>
    <p>结构论点增强，不代表垂直上涨后的战术设置一定良好。</p>
    <p>若通胀持续过热、美联储以更高实际收益率回应，黄金可以大幅调整；若美元与实际收益率一起上涨，调整可以很猛烈。</p>
    <p>这不会自动推翻长期论点，只意味着通向更大货币调整的路径，可以包含央行成功紧缩的一段时期。</p>
    <p>所以我们更愿把黄金当作<strong>信号资产</strong>：它最清楚地显示市场是否越来越不愿持有长期名义债权。但最干净的信号也会超买。结构信念不能替代入场纪律。</p>
    <h3>白银：带工业引擎的货币贝塔</h3>
    <p>白银常被描述为上行更大的黄金，过于简单。</p>
    <p>白银同时包含货币属性与重要工业属性，在温和宽松体制中拥有更大凸性。若实际收益率下降、美元走弱、全球活动健康，白银可以大幅跑赢黄金。</p>
    <p>但同一结构也使其在信用事故中更脆弱：工业需求预期可以下降，杠杆可以解除，流动性可以消失，白银可以比黄金跌得快得多。</p>
    <p>因此，我们的层级是：<strong>黄金 = 更干净的货币信号；白银 = 更高贝塔的货币表达。</strong>两者不应互换。</p>
    <h3>铂金与钯金：标签遮住基本面</h3>
    <p>铂金和钯金都被归入贵金属，但物理前景越来越不同。</p>
    <p>铂金的中期供需平衡更有吸引力，库存受限，持续短缺概率更高；钯金因汽车需求长期转型与潜在过剩，结构背景更困难。</p>
    <p>因此，我们偏好的相对判断是：<strong>铂金优于钯金。</strong></p>
    <p>这不是预测铂金每月上涨，也不是说钯金不会逼空。供应中断、空头回补或地缘事件都能让钯金暴涨，但战术逼空与结构性短缺不是同一投资论点。PGM 应按物理平衡分析，而不是按“贵金属”三个字分析。</p>
    <h3>铜：最好的结构故事，也可能是坏入场点</h3>
    <p>铜仍是组合中最强的长期工业稀缺故事之一。需求异常广泛：AI 数据中心需要电气基础设施，电网需要加固，发电需要输电，机器人需要电机与线缆，电气化和国防都需要铜；矿山供给则要多年才能开发。</p>
    <p>长期设置强大，却不意味着每个价格都有吸引力。</p>
    <p>近期铜挤压说明，物理紧张、仓库仓位与投机结构可以把市场推到长期投资者不应舒服追逐的水平。</p>
    <p>这再次说明：<strong>结构性稀缺与战术入场是两个问题。</strong></p>
    <p>最好的铜机会可能在市场消化剧烈挤压之后，而不是当中。论点仍强，紧迫性不强。</p>
  </div>

  <div class="pod-copy l-en">
    <h3>Bitcoin: the liquidity clock moved before the calendar</h3>
    <p>Bitcoin is the asset where our forecasting process changed the most. The earlier framework gave significant weight to the historical four-year cycle and the idea that a major trough would probably occur in the October-to-December 2026 window.</p>
    <p>That view was not irrational. Past Bitcoin cycles have shown strong temporal patterns. Miner economics matter. Speculative leverage matters. Halving narratives matter. Behavioral reflexivity matters.</p>
    <p>But the 2026 market is structurally different from the earlier cycles used to build that analogy. Bitcoin now trades through institutional vehicles. It responds directly to macro asset allocation. Stablecoins provide a much larger settlement base. Corporate balance sheets hold the asset. Regulation matters. Treasury-market policy matters. The investor base is more macro-sensitive.</p>
    <p>That means a future liquidity transition can be front-run. And that is exactly what appears to have happened. The policy catalyst we expected later began arriving earlier. The market moved before the old cycle date.</p>
    <p>That does not mean the four-year cycle has disappeared. It means the cycle clock is no longer the only clock.</p>
    <h3>The six Bitcoin clocks</h3>
    <p>We would now rank Bitcoin's governing variables roughly like this.</p>
    <p>The first is the <strong>dollar regime</strong>. A weaker dollar generally improves the environment for alternative monetary assets.</p>
    <p>The second is <strong>real yields</strong>. Falling real yields reduce the opportunity cost of non-yielding or alternative monetary assets.</p>
    <p>The third is <strong>Treasury and Fed liquidity architecture</strong>. This includes more than conventional QE. Changes in market functioning, duration pressure and expected policy can alter crypto pricing before a central bank formally cuts.</p>
    <p>The fourth is <strong>stablecoin liquidity</strong>. A larger digital-dollar base can improve settlement liquidity and the capacity of the crypto system to absorb risk.</p>
    <p>The fifth is <strong>ETF and institutional flows</strong>. These turn traditional asset allocation directly into spot demand or supply.</p>
    <p>The sixth is the <strong>historical cycle calendar</strong>. Still useful. No longer sovereign.</p>
    <p>That hierarchy explains why the old October forecast lost authority without requiring us to pretend historical cycles never mattered.</p>
    <h3>Bitcoin is not gold</h3>
    <p>Gold and Bitcoin share a monetary story. They do not share the same risk profile.</p>
    <p>Gold is held by central banks and conservative pools of capital. Bitcoin contains more leverage, reflexivity and speculative risk. That difference determines the sequencing in a stress event.</p>
    <p>In a managed easing or repression regime: gold can rise; Bitcoin can rise faster.</p>
    <p>In a genuine liquidity accident: Bitcoin can fall violently first. Gold can also fall as investors raise cash, but it should generally stabilize earlier. After policy responds and liquidity improves, Bitcoin can recover later with more beta.</p>
    <p>This is why calling Bitcoin an immediate hedge against every Treasury-market problem is dangerous. It is better understood as a <strong>high-beta monetary optionality asset</strong>.</p>
    <p>Its long-run thesis can strengthen because of a fiscal or monetary regime change while its short-run price collapses during the liquidity event that forces that regime change. Both can be true.</p>
    <h3>Stablecoins connect Bitcoin to Treasury without backing Bitcoin</h3>
    <p>The growing stablecoin system creates a particularly interesting bridge. Treasury bills back stablecoin reserves. Stablecoins provide liquidity inside crypto markets. Crypto activity increases demand for stablecoins. Stablecoin growth can increase demand for Treasury bills. The result is a financial loop connecting digital-asset market liquidity to U.S. sovereign collateral.</p>
    <p>Bitcoin remains economically separate from that collateral. It is not backed by Treasury bills. But the liquidity system surrounding it increasingly is.</p>
    <p>That makes crypto less detached from conventional finance than the ideological language around it often suggests. The more regulated stablecoins grow, the more the crypto ecosystem can become intertwined with the U.S. Treasury market. That is one reason the next crypto cycle is likely to look different from the last.</p>
    <h3>Ethereum and the rest of crypto need a stricter standard</h3>
    <p>Bitcoin can retain a monetary thesis without generating application revenue. Most other crypto assets cannot rely on that same argument.</p>
    <p>Smart-contract networks need economic throughput. Stablecoin settlement. Tokenized assets. Applications. Fees. Developer activity. Real usage.</p>
    <p>That makes the next crypto cycle a selection problem similar to AI. The question is no longer simply: <strong>Bitcoin rises, therefore everything else should rise more.</strong></p>
    <blockquote>Which networks actually capture economic value from the growth of digital-dollar and tokenized-finance activity?</blockquote>
    <p>That will matter much more in a regulated institutional market than it did during earlier speculative cycles.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pod-copy l-zh">
    <h3>比特币：流动性时钟先于日历移动</h3>
    <p>比特币是我们预测过程变化最大的资产。旧框架高度重视历史四年周期，并认为重大低点大概会出现在 2026 年 10 至 12 月窗口。</p>
    <p>这个判断并非不理性。过去比特币周期表现出强时间模式。矿工经济性、投机杠杆、减半叙事与行为反身性都重要。</p>
    <p>但 2026 年市场与构建类比的早期周期有结构差异。比特币现在通过机构载体交易，直接回应宏观资产配置，稳定币提供更大结算基础，企业资产负债表持币，监管与美债市场政策都重要，投资者基础对宏观更敏感。</p>
    <p>因此，未来流动性转折可以被提前交易。事情看起来正是如此：我们预期稍后到来的政策催化提前出现，市场在旧周期日期之前就已移动。</p>
    <p>这不意味着四年周期消失，而是周期时钟不再是唯一时钟。</p>
    <h3>比特币的六只时钟</h3>
    <p>现在我们会大致如此排列比特币的支配变量。</p>
    <p>第一是<strong>美元体制</strong>。美元走弱通常改善替代货币资产环境。</p>
    <p>第二是<strong>实际收益率</strong>。实际收益率下降，降低无收益或替代货币资产的机会成本。</p>
    <p>第三是<strong>财政部与美联储流动性架构</strong>。它不只包括传统 QE；市场功能、久期压力与预期政策的变化，可以在央行正式降息前改变加密资产定价。</p>
    <p>第四是<strong>稳定币流动性</strong>。更大的数字美元基础可以改善结算流动性，提高加密系统吸收风险的能力。</p>
    <p>第五是<strong>ETF 与机构资金流</strong>。它把传统资产配置直接转化为现货需求或供给。</p>
    <p>第六是<strong>历史周期日历</strong>。仍有用，不再拥有最高权威。</p>
    <p>这个层级解释了旧 10 月预测为何失去权威，同时无需假装历史周期从未重要。</p>
    <h3>比特币不是黄金</h3>
    <p>黄金与比特币共享货币故事，却不共享风险属性。</p>
    <p>黄金由央行与保守资本池持有；比特币包含更多杠杆、反身性与投机风险。这个差别决定压力事件中的顺序。</p>
    <p>在受管理的宽松或压抑体制中，黄金可以上涨，比特币可以涨得更快。</p>
    <p>在真正流动性事故中，比特币可以先暴跌；黄金也会因投资者筹集现金而跌，但通常更早稳定。政策回应、流动性改善后，比特币可以稍后以更大贝塔恢复。</p>
    <p>所以，把比特币称为每一次美债市场问题的即时对冲很危险。更好的理解是：<strong>高贝塔货币期权性资产</strong>。</p>
    <p>它的长期论点可以因财政或货币体制变化而增强，而短期价格又在迫使体制变化的流动性事件中坍塌。两者都可以成立。</p>
    <h3>稳定币连接比特币与美债，却不为比特币提供支持资产</h3>
    <p>增长中的稳定币系统创造一座有趣桥梁：国库券支持稳定币储备，稳定币为加密市场提供流动性，加密活动提高稳定币需求，稳定币增长又可以增加国库券需求。结果是一条把数字资产市场流动性连接到美国主权抵押品的金融循环。</p>
    <p>比特币在经济上仍与该抵押品分离。它不由国库券支持，但环绕它的流动性系统越来越多地由国库券支持。</p>
    <p>这使加密市场不像其意识形态语言所暗示的那样脱离传统金融。受监管稳定币越增长，加密生态就越与美国国债市场交织。这也是下一轮加密周期很可能不同于上一轮的原因。</p>
    <h3>以太坊与其他加密资产需要更严格标准</h3>
    <p>比特币可以不产生应用收入而保留货币论点，多数其他加密资产却不能依赖同一论据。</p>
    <p>智能合约网络需要经济吞吐：稳定币结算、代币化资产、应用、费用、开发者活动与真实使用。</p>
    <p>因此，下一轮加密周期成为类似 AI 的筛选问题，不再只是<strong>比特币上涨，所以其他一切应该涨得更多</strong>。</p>
    <blockquote>哪些网络真正从数字美元与代币化金融活动增长中捕获经济价值？</blockquote>
    <p>在受监管的机构市场中，这比在早期投机周期中重要得多。</p>
  </div>

  <p>{{ t('The current regime therefore produces a more nuanced map.', '因此，当前体制产生了一张更细腻的地图。') }}</p>
