  <div class="pod-copy">
    <p>{{ t('The final task is to convert all of this into a forward map. Not a calendar prophecy. A regime tree. What happens if policymakers successfully manage duration pressure? What happens if the market solves the problem without policy? What happens if inflation refuses to cooperate? And what happens if the duration stress finally enters credit? Those four futures are where the article turns from diagnosis to forecast.',
      '最后的任务，是把这一切转换成前瞻地图。不是日历预言，而是一棵体制树：如果政策制定者成功管理久期压力会怎样？如果市场无需政策就解决问题会怎样？如果通胀拒绝配合会怎样？如果久期压力最终进入信用又会怎样？这四种未来，是文章从诊断转向预测的地方。') }}</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="regimes"><span class="num">9</span>{{ t('Four futures from here', '从此出发的四种未来') }}</h2>
  <div class="pod-copy l-en">
    <p>A forecast becomes more useful when it tells the reader how it can fail. That is the main repair we are making to the old Mastermind process.</p>
    <p>Our previous reports often expressed a base case with enough specificity that the path itself began to acquire too much authority. The market then did what markets do: it respected some mechanisms, ignored some dates and introduced new evidence that should have changed the path faster than the narrative did.</p>
    <p>The better approach is to define a small number of regimes and then let observable variables move probability from one regime to another.</p>
    <p>As of August 24, 2026, we see four plausible futures.</p>
    <p>These are not statistical confidence intervals. They are research-desk probabilities: a disciplined way to make our priors explicit and force ourselves to update them when the evidence changes.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pod-copy l-zh">
    <p>当预测告诉读者它会如何失败时，它才更有用。这是我们对旧 Mastermind 方法做的核心修复。</p>
    <p>以前的报告往往把基准路径写得过于具体，以致路径本身获得了过多权威。市场随后做了市场一贯会做的事：遵循一些机制，忽略一些日期，并提供了本应让路径比叙事更快调整的新证据。</p>
    <p>更好的做法是定义少数几种体制，再让可观察变量在它们之间移动概率。截至 2026 年 8 月 24 日，我们看到四种合理未来。这些不是统计置信区间，而是研究台概率：一种把先验摆到台面上，并迫使我们在证据变化时更新的纪律。</p>
  </div>

