  <h2 id="triggers"><span class="num">10</span>{{ t('The trigger framework', '触发框架') }}</h2>
  <div class="pod-copy l-en">
    <p>The next step is to define the evidence that would make us change our mind.</p>
    <p>The levels below are not magical technical boundaries. They are operating thresholds designed to force a research update. We care much more about combinations than individual prints.</p>
    <h3>Long Treasury yields</h3>
    <p>The 30-year yield is the first gauge. A move sustainably below roughly 5% without larger support would favor Benign Absorption. A move around 5.0–5.4% is uncomfortable but still consistent with Managed Duration Pressure. A move above roughly 5.5–5.6% that persists while Treasury support fails would materially increase the probability of a Term-Premium Accident. The exact level matters less than whether the market can find willing private buyers without increasingly active intervention.</p>
    <h3>Real yields</h3>
    <p>The 10-year real yield tells us whether monetary conditions are becoming more or less restrictive. A sustained move below roughly 2.25% would support the easing side of the framework. A move above roughly 2.55% would materially strengthen the Inflation Veto branch. The key is not one session. It is direction plus persistence.</p>
    <h3>Breakeven inflation</h3>
    <p>The breakeven rate helps distinguish high nominal yields caused by real compensation from those driven by inflation expectations. A long yield rising because real yields are rising is different from a long yield rising because investors are demanding more inflation compensation. Both can hurt equities. They imply different policy constraints.</p>
    <h3>Credit spreads</h3>
    <p>Broad high-yield OAS is the most important transmission gauge. As long as broad spreads remain tight, the duration problem is mostly a valuation and allocation problem. If they begin widening through roughly 3.5% and continue toward 4% or higher, the probability of systemic transmission rises. The weakest credits should move first. That makes CCC spreads a useful early warning even while the broad index remains calm.</p>
    <h3>VIX and breadth</h3>
    <p>Volatility needs to become persistent to confirm a crisis. A one-day VIX spike is not enough. A VIX that stays above the mid-20s while breadth deteriorates and credit spreads widen is a different state. Again, the combination is what matters.</p>
    <h3>The dollar</h3>
    <p>The dollar is most informative when read against yields. Long yields rising with a strong dollar is conventional tightening. Long yields rising with a weak dollar is the more dangerous signal because investors are asking for more compensation while showing less enthusiasm for the currency exposure. That is the quadrant that would make the duration-confidence thesis more urgent.</p>
    <h3>AI credit</h3>
    <p>AI corporate spreads are the bridge between the sovereign story and the technology story. If tech issuance remains large but easily absorbed, the boom can continue. If investors begin demanding large concessions, spreads widen materially and project financing becomes harder, the cost of capital starts directly rationing AI investment. That would be one of the clearest signs that the duration problem had moved from macro backdrop to real-economy selection mechanism.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="pod-copy l-zh">
    <p>下一步是定义哪些证据会让我们改变看法。下列水平不是神奇的技术边界，而是用来强制研究更新的操作阈值。我们对变量组合的重视，远高于单一数据点。</p>
    <h3>长期美债收益率</h3>
    <p>30 年期收益率是第一仪表。若无需更大支持就持续低于约 5%，将支持良性吸收；5.0–5.4% 不舒服，但仍符合受管理的久期压力；若持续超过约 5.5–5.6%，同时财政部支持失效，则期限溢价事故概率显著上升。比精确点位更重要的，是市场能否在无需日益积极干预下找到自愿私人买家。</p>
    <h3>实际收益率</h3>
    <p>10 年期实际收益率告诉我们货币条件正变得更还是更少限制。持续低于约 2.25% 支持宽松侧；超过约 2.55% 将显著强化通胀否决分支。关键不是一个交易日，而是方向加持续性。</p>
    <h3>盈亏平衡通胀率</h3>
    <p>盈亏平衡通胀率有助于区分高名义收益率来自实际回报补偿，还是通胀预期。因实际收益率上升而升的长端，与因投资者要求更高通胀补偿而升的长端不同。两者都会伤害股票，却意味着不同政策约束。</p>
    <h3>信用利差</h3>
    <p>广义高收益债 OAS 是最重要的传导仪表。只要广义利差仍紧，久期问题主要还是估值与配置问题。若突破约 3.5% 并继续走向 4% 或更高，系统性传导概率上升。最弱信用应先行，所以即使广义指数平静，CCC 利差也是有用的早期预警。</p>
    <h3>VIX 与市场广度</h3>
    <p>波动率必须持续才能确认危机。一日 VIX 飙升不够；若 VIX 在 20 多点中段以上维持，市场广度恶化、信用利差走阔，就是另一种状态。再次，组合才重要。</p>
    <h3>美元</h3>
    <p>美元与收益率一起读取时最有信息量。长端与强美元同升是传统紧缩；长端与弱美元同升更危险，因为投资者要求更多补偿，却对货币暴露更没热情。这个象限会让久期信心论点更紧迫。</p>
    <h3>AI 信用</h3>
    <p>AI 企业利差是主权故事与科技故事之间的桥。若科技发债仍大但轻松被吸收，热潮可继续；若投资者开始要求大幅让步，利差实质走阔，项目融资更困难，资本成本就开始直接配给 AI 投资。这将是久期问题从宏观背景进入实体经济筛选机制的最清晰信号之一。</p>
  </div>

