    <h3>Evidence labels for implementation</h3>
    <p>Each important claim should retain one of four labels in source metadata:</p>
    <p><strong>[F] Fact</strong> — Directly observed, official or independently verified. <strong>[C] Consensus / Reported</strong> — Credible reporting that Mastermind has not independently proven. <strong>[I] Inference</strong> — Mastermind's causal interpretation. <strong>[S] Scenario</strong> — Forward-looking conditional judgment or desk probability.</p>
    <h3>Claims that must remain explicitly inference or scenario</h3>
    <p>The following should never be presented as established fact: Treasury has a specific unannounced long-yield pain threshold; stablecoins will materially reduce long-end Treasury supply pressure; AI corporate borrowing is already a dominant cause of Treasury term premium; Managed Duration Pressure will remain the base regime; Gold's current rally is primarily a fiscal/duration-confidence signal; the October Bitcoin trough has been front-run; a successful 2026 containment phase will produce a 2027 AI blow-off; any precise probability assigned to the four future regimes.</p>
    <h3>Production-day refresh requirement</h3>
    <p>Before publication, refresh: 30-year Treasury yield; 10-year nominal yield; 10-year real yield; 10-year breakeven; DXY; VIX; broad HY OAS; CCC HY OAS; gold; Bitcoin; silver; platinum; palladium; copper; relevant equity/index prices; any forecast probability that depends on data released after August 24.</p>
    <p>The article should preserve the research date while clearly timestamping any refreshed market snapshot.</p>
