    <p>{{ t('The market is not yet in a credit crisis. It is in something more interesting: <strong>the cost of long-term capital has risen enough to begin disciplining the AI buildout and the sovereign financing system at the same time.</strong> Gold is reacting before conventional easing arrives, Bitcoin&rsquo;s liquidity clock has moved ahead of the old cycle calendar, and equities are beginning to separate according to capital efficiency rather than AI narrative alone. The next phase depends on whether the long end stabilizes naturally, is managed through Treasury and market structure, stays pinned by inflation, or finally transmits into credit.',
      '市场尚未陷入信用危机。它正处于更耐人寻味的阶段：<strong>长期资本成本已上升到足以同时约束 AI 建设与主权融资体系的程度。</strong>黄金在传统宽松到来前已作出反应；比特币的流动性时钟走在旧周期日历之前；股票也开始按资本效率分化，而不再只按 AI 叙事分化。下一阶段取决于长端收益率是自然稳定、通过财政部与市场结构得到管理、被通胀钉住，还是最终传导进信用。') }}</p>
