  <h2 id="duration-mechanism"><span class="num">3</span>{{ t('The price of duration', '久期的价格') }}</h2>
  <div class="pod-section-kicker">{{ t('The governing mechanism · one auction for long-term capital', '治理全局的机制 · 一场长期资本拍卖') }}</div>
  <div class="pod-intro-grid">
    <div class="pod-copy">
      <p>{{ t('To understand why the current market feels internally contradictory, stop thinking of interest rates as something the Federal Reserve simply &ldquo;sets.&rdquo; The Fed controls a very short-term policy rate. <strong>The market determines the price of lending money for ten, twenty or thirty years.</strong>',
        '要理解当前市场为何内在矛盾，就别再把利率想成美联储简单“设定”的数字。美联储控制的是极短期政策利率；<strong>借出十年、二十年或三十年资金的价格，由市场决定。</strong>') }}</p>
      <p>{{ t('A long-term investor accepts decades of inflation risk, fiscal risk, opportunity cost and uncertainty. When duration supply rises—or buyers become less willing to hold it at the old yield—the yield must rise until the market clears.',
        '长期投资者承担的是数十年的通胀风险、财政风险、机会成本与不确定性。当久期供给上升，或买家不再愿意按原有收益率持有时，收益率必须上升，直到市场完成出清。') }}</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="pod-mechanism-card">
      <span class="mk">{{ t('The clearing equation', '出清方程') }}</span>
      <strong>{{ t('Borrowers&rsquo; duration demand = investors&rsquo; willingness to absorb it', '借款人的久期需求 = 投资者吸收久期的意愿') }}</strong>
      <p>{{ t('The yield is the price that forces both sides to meet. It is simultaneously a funding cost, a discount rate and a policy constraint.', '收益率是迫使双方相遇的价格。它同时是融资成本、折现率与政策约束。') }}</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
  <div data-figure-slot="fig-collision"></div>
  <div class="pod-loop" aria-label="AI duration feedback loop">
    <div class="pod-loop-step"><b>{{ t('AI demand', 'AI 需求') }}</b><small>{{ t('More physical buildout', '更多实体建设') }}</small></div>
    <div class="pod-loop-step"><b>{{ t('Capex rises', '资本开支上升') }}</b><small>{{ t('Power, chips, buildings', '电力、芯片、建筑') }}</small></div>
    <div class="pod-loop-step"><b>{{ t('Financing rises', '融资上升') }}</b><small>{{ t('Debt and project capital', '债务与项目资本') }}</small></div>
    <div class="pod-loop-step"><b>{{ t('Duration supply', '久期供给') }}</b><small>{{ t('Beside Treasury issuance', '叠加财政部发行') }}</small></div>
    <div class="pod-loop-step"><b>{{ t('Yield rises', '收益率上升') }}</b><small>{{ t('Investors demand more', '投资者要求更多补偿') }}</small></div>
    <div class="pod-loop-step"><b>{{ t('Projects selected', '项目被筛选') }}</b><small>{{ t('ROI must clear the hurdle', '回报必须越过门槛') }}</small></div>
  </div>
  <p>{{ t('AI is no longer only affected by rates. Its financing demand increasingly participates in the market that sets them. The boom begins raising the hurdle rate that values the boom itself. <sup class="ev ev-i">I</sup>',
    'AI 已不再只是被动承受利率影响；它的融资需求正越来越多地参与决定利率的市场。繁荣开始抬高衡量自身价值的门槛收益率。<sup class="ev ev-i">I</sup>') }}</p>
  <div class="pod-stage-band">
    <div class="pod-stage" style="--stage:var(--pod-teal)"><b>{{ t('First AI phase', 'AI 第一阶段') }}</b><p>{{ t('Scarcity wins. GPU, HBM and network bottlenecks dominate.', '稀缺取胜。GPU、HBM 与网络瓶颈主导。') }}</p></div>
    <div class="pod-stage" style="--stage:var(--pod-gold)"><b>{{ t('Current transition', '当前过渡期') }}</b><p>{{ t('Financing pressure rises. FCF, dilution and duration begin separating names.', '融资压力上升。自由现金流、稀释与久期开始区分公司。') }}</p></div>
    <div class="pod-stage" style="--stage:var(--pod-blue)"><b>{{ t('Next AI phase', 'AI 下一阶段') }}</b><p>{{ t('Return on capital wins. Weak projects die; cash-flow proof dominates.', '资本回报取胜。弱项目退出，现金流证据主导。') }}</p></div>
  </div>
  <h3>{{ t('Why the long bond suddenly matters to equity investors', '为什么长期债券突然对股票投资者至关重要') }}</h3>
  <p>{{ t('The same future profit is worth less when investors can earn a higher return elsewhere. That is why Nvidia can report extraordinary demand and still experience multiple compression if long yields rise. A company can be <strong>fundamentally right and still be a bad stock at the wrong price.</strong>',
    '当投资者能在别处获得更高回报时，同一笔未来利润的现值就更低。这就是为什么英伟达即使报告非凡需求，也可能在长端收益率上升时遭遇估值倍数压缩。企业可以<strong>在基本面上正确，却在错误价格上成为一只糟糕的股票。</strong>') }}</p>
  <p>{{ t('Expensive money can strengthen the survivors: weak projects are cancelled, duplicative capacity is delayed and companies with genuine demand plus internal financing keep investing. If real rates later fall, the survivors enter the next phase with more infrastructure, less competition and visibly better economics.',
    '昂贵资金反而可能强化幸存者：弱项目被取消，重复产能被推迟，拥有真实需求与内部融资能力的公司继续投资。若实际利率随后下降，幸存者将带着更多基础设施、更少竞争与更清晰的经济性进入下一阶段。') }}</p>
  <h2 id="policy-trap-v2"><span class="num">4</span>{{ t('Dalio, Treasury, and the policy trap', '达利欧、财政部与政策困局') }}</h2>
  <div class="pod-section-kicker">{{ t('Reaction functions · plumbing is not monetization', '反应函数 · 市场管道不等于货币化') }}</div>
  <p>{{ t('A government can carry enormous debt for a long time while buyers willingly absorb it at an acceptable yield. The critical transition comes when debt supply grows faster than demand at the prevailing price. Then the market clears through a higher yield—and that higher yield raises the government&rsquo;s own refinancing cost.',
    '只要买家愿意按可接受的收益率吸收债务，政府就能长期承载庞大债务。关键转折出现在债务供给以现行价格计增长得比需求更快时；市场随后通过更高收益率出清，而更高收益率又抬升政府自身的再融资成本。') }}</p>
  <div class="pod-table-wrap"><table class="pod-table pod-compact">
    <thead><tr><th>{{ t('Already visible', '已经可见') }}</th><th>{{ t('Not proven today', '今天尚未证明') }}</th></tr></thead>
