    <p>{{ t('The first phase of the AI boom rewarded the company closest to scarcity. There were not enough accelerators, then not enough HBM, optical networking, power, cooling or transformer capacity. When demand hits a hard bottleneck, the economics are easy: <strong>the scarce supplier wins.</strong>',
      'AI 热潮第一阶段奖励的是最靠近稀缺性的公司。先是加速器不够，继而是 HBM、光网络、电力、冷却与变压器产能不足。当需求撞上硬瓶颈时，经济逻辑很简单：<strong>稀缺供应商取胜。</strong>') }}</p>
    <p>{{ t('That phase is becoming less forgiving. The market is beginning to ask a different question: <strong>how much durable cash flow does each additional dollar of AI investment actually create?</strong> This is the transition from AI exposure to AI capital efficiency.',
      '这一阶段正变得不再宽容。市场开始追问一个不同的问题：<strong>每多投入一美元 AI 资本，究竟能创造多少持久现金流？</strong>这就是从 AI 敞口转向 AI 资本效率。') }}</p>
